===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|coinage by Q3743255}}
{{coin|en|Q3743255|in=1910|nobycat=1}}, from {{lbor|en|grc|μωρόν|notext=1}}, the neuter form of {{m|grc|μωρός|t=foolish, dull}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q193607}} {{lb|en|informal|derogatory}} A [[stupid]] person; an [[idiot]]; a [[fool]].
#: {{syn|en|imbecile<id:Q193607>|idiot<id:Q193607>|retard<id:Q193607><qq:offensive>|maroon|Thesaurus:fool|Thesaurus:idiot}}
#* {{RQ:Hemingway Sun Also Rises|passage=“I misjudged you,” Harvey said. You’re not a '''moron'''. You’re only a case of arrested development. }}
# {{senseid|en|person with Q183560}} {{lb|en|psychology|dated|originally}} A person of mild mental subnormality in the former classification of mental retardation, having an intelligence quotient of 50–70.
#: {{syn|en|imbecile<id:person with Q183560>|idiot<id:person with Q183560>|retard<id:person with Q183560><qq:offensive>}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The current medical term for having an IQ between 50 and 70 is “mild [[intellectual disability]]”.

